MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_001: What is it that you wanted to talk about, Lysander?
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_002: I wanted to hear your thoughts on Bertrand, the new\nking of Brezarant.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_003: Eh... My thoughts? Whatever for?
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_004: Well, I was curious, so I asked the Brezarant troops\nhow he ended up taking the Trial of the Chariot.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_005: And they told me his last battle as a general of Arago\nwas none other than the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_006: Ah.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_007: You began as a knight in service to a Cydonian\nnoble, or so I hear. So I wondered...
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_008: I see. It's no secret that I lost the house I served\nduring that massacre. As well as my family.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_009: And now you'd like to know if that colors my opinion\nof the king of Brezarant.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_010: I know that you're a proud knight.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_011: Which might give you a grudge against Bertrand,\ngiven that he's responsible for your lord's death.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_012: Mind you, the soldiers all agree that wasn't entirely\nhis fault.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_013: But for someone like you with a personal stake,\nI could see it being hard to put your feelings aside.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_014: Hehe...hehehe.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_015: Hmm? Did I say something funny?
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_016: Forgive me! I just can't decide if I should be pleased\nto hear such high praise from a noble of Saramis...
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_017: or if I should be offended that he would make such\na cruel presumption. Perhaps it's a little of both.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_018: What do you mean by that?
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_019: I am, as you say, a proud knight. However, I daresay\nthat's no reason for me to hold a grudge.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_020: Of course, there are some who might swear revenge\nin such cases. My acquaintance Suarez, for example.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_021: But as I see it, long-held revenge is nothing more\nthan a way to relive one's past defeat.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_022: A true knight should only blame their former self\nand use that as motivation to keep improving.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_023: Since the Cydonia Massacre, I've honed my skills and\nbecome all the stronger.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_024: Of course. Forgive me for doubting you based on\nyour history rather than your character.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_025: I admire your way of thinking and your perspective\non your own honor. So I shall take my leave.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_026: Hm? He's gone already?
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_027: That's all he wanted? I was expecting a confession of\nlove at the very least.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_028: Lysander may be highborn and good-looking, but\nhe's clearly stubborn and unaccommodating.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_C_029: Hmph. How vexing. I'll just have to put this anger\nto work in today's training.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_001: Where shall I eat today? There are so many choices.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_002: Ah, pardon me. Wait, Catania?
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_003: Hm? Oh, Lysander... It's no matter. I'm fine.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_004: Are you really fine? If you're unwell, we should\nfetch a doctor.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_005: I said I was fine. And I believe I am perfectly\ncapable of assessing my own condition.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_006: O-of course.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_007: In that case, I was on my way to a meal. Would you\nlike to join me?
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_008: Oh? Unfortunately I can't.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_009: I've, um, already eaten. So long!
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_010: She must still be cross with me after my\nthoughtlessness last time.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_011: Hmm?
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_012: Oh, I hope he didn't hear that.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_013: I...couldn't help but notice your stomach rumbling.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_014: Of course you did! Go ahead, then. Laugh. Mock.\nDo your worst!
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_015: There's no way you'll ever consider me a "proud\nknight" after this, I'm sure. *sob*
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_016: No, I wasn't making fun of you! Please don't cry.\nIf you haven't eaten yet, it's my treat.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_017: You must have been hungry indeed to eat so much.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_018: Please forgive me. My finances have been a bit...\nstretched of late.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_019: Before I ran into you, I was planning to enjoy the\nsavory aromas of the food and then return home.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_020: But why? You're well paid, or so I assume, and you\ndon't strike me as a glutton.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_021: I'm in your debt for your kindness today. I suppose\nyou have a right to an explanation.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_022: As the battles have been getting fiercer lately,\nmy equipment has been losing its luster.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_023: As you know, it's unseemly to wear damaged\narmor, so I've been replacing it more frequently.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_024: That would explain it. I've noticed how pristine\nyour equipment is at all times.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_025: I know, I know. It's humiliating. I'm terrible for\ncaring so much about the sheen on my armor.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_026: I don't think so. On the contrary, I admire that you\ntake pride in how you present yourself.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_027: You...admire me? Well, I...well.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_028: I have a proposal that might solve your issue. Would\nyou consider training some of the Saramis troops?
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_029: We'd provide the weaponry. And you'd be paid an\ninstructor's fee, of course.
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_030: They could learn much from a proud knight such as\nyourself. Consider it, won't you?
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_031: Hm... How could I possibly refuse a request from\nyou? I happily accept!
MID_SE_Lys_Cat_B_032: Now, about that "instructor's fee." Is it negotiable?